# loop — environment template
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in what you use:
#
#   cp .env.sample .env
#
# How loop treats .env (internal/dotenv):
#   · ./.env is loaded on every command; the file named by LOOP_ENV_FILE
#     is loaded after it.
#   · Your real shell environment always wins — files only fill gaps.
#     Between the two files, ./.env wins over $LOOP_ENV_FILE.
#   · One KEY=VALUE per line. An "export " prefix, single/double quotes,
#     and trailing "  # comments" are all handled; malformed lines warn
#     with file:line and are skipped.
#   · .env is gitignored — keep real keys here, never in pipeline/room
#     YAML (those get committed and shared).

# ── Provider API keys ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One of these is required for any pipeline stage or room persona that
# uses the matching provider. Unused ones can stay empty.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Custom providers via base_url (provider: openai + base_url) often use
# their own key name. Set `api_key_env: GROQ_API_KEY` in the YAML, then
# define it here — any name works:
#
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OLLAMA_API_KEY=

# Local endpoints that need no auth (e.g. base_url: http://localhost:11434)
# don't need a key at all.

# ── loop knobs (all optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────

# Extra env file loaded after ./.env. Handy for a shared team file or a
# per-project override chain. Paths are used as-is (no ~ expansion).
#
# LOOP_ENV_FILE=

# Node binary the cline executor should run (default: "node" on PATH).
# The SDK needs Node >= 22 — point this at a newer binary if your system
# node is older, e.g.:
#
# LOOP_NODE=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@24/bin/node

# Override where the cline host script lives. Default resolution order:
#   1. this variable
#   2. ~/.loop/executors/cline/index.mjs   (what `loop executor install cline` writes)
#   3. ./host/loop-cline-host/index.mjs    (repo-local dev checkout)
#
# LOOP_CLINE_HOST=
